id=a52sxq_adreno_driver
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Adreno GPU driver selector (V@0530 stock default, V@0530.55 / V@0849 / V@0863 built in, user drivers)
author=kusti420
description=The A14 vendor ships the Adreno 642L userspace driver V@0530.0 (11/22/21), which stays in /vendor untouched and is the default (testers asked for it back). Built in, as complete 64-bit sets under /vendor/k4gpu (every v<id>/ directory here, pinned by its SHA256SUMS): V@0530.55.1 (05/11/25, Samsung stock from A528BXXSBGYI3), V@0849.0 (09/19/25, community module by @sudami) and V@0863.1 (12/24/25, "Adreno GPU Driver 863.1" module by @Joshaby), each with its a660 SQE microcode. Settings > ZineUI > UI > GPU driver writes persist.sys.k4.gpu_driver; /system/etc/init/k4_gpu_driver.rc overlays the selected set over /vendor/lib64 at early-boot (before the first /dev/kgsl-3d0 open, which loads the microcode), binds its microcode and, for V@07xx+ builds, the Vulkan 1.3 feature file (V@0530 builds report Vulkan 1.1), and reports sys.k4.gpu_active. User drivers: k4-gpu-driver (post-fs-data, own SELinux domain k4gpu) imports Adreno driver modules (KernelSU/Magisk, system/vendor/lib64 layout; metamodule-era KernelSU mounts nothing without a metamodule, so no Mountify is needed; the ROM's default metamodule, its build of meta-overlayfs, leaves driver modules to the selector, so they are imported too) and drivers added in Settings (Add driver: a zip, validated and staged by Settings) into /data/k4gpu/store and binds the selected one the same way; a new driver module is selected with a trial boot; a module already mounted by the root manager wins and is only reported; with KernelSU no metamodule (meta-overlayfs, Mountify, magic mount, ...) mounts a driver module at all - mounted with KernelSU's label vendor_file one bootlooped the phone and bypassed the failsafe - because k4-gpu-driver guard (KernelSU's domain) gives each one a skip_mount file right before ksud's post-fs-data, from the end of init.rc and from /data/adb/post-fs-data.d (written by the ROM's metamodule hook), so it is imported here with the stock labels and a trial boot also on the first boot after its install. A boot with a newly selected driver that never reaches boot_completed falls back to V@0530.0 on the next boot (persist.sys.k4.gpu_trial / gpu_failed); a missing or damaged user driver falls back too (sys.k4.gpu_missing). Only userspace libraries and the unsigned a660 SQE are ever bound, never signed firmware (zap, GMU). Benchmarks 2026-10-20 (3DMark, same start temperatures): V@0849 +5% GL / +8% Vulkan graphics, same clocks and heat, 0 GPU faults on both. The 32-bit V@0530 libs stay (no 32-bit process uses the GPU).
